      "comment": "MALDINI (3) brings the sharpest recent form after going under by beaten half a length in BM80 company at Morphettville Parks, where he raced wide throughout and was still only pipped at the post. The return from Saturday company reads well for this and expect a big run. KIKORANGI (5) is the obvious threat after consecutive wins, the latest a two-length BM68 success at Morphettville on soft ground, and his record around 1800m gives him solid grounding despite the grade rise. MR TRAFFICANTI (6) made solid inroads last start and is one win and one place from three starts at this track and distance, with Tala Hutchinson a proven partner. JILLADORA (2) was plain when ninth last start, yet her Gawler third in Open grade two back keeps her in the mix if she handles 1800m for the first time.",
